# Dienogest + 10 Acetone: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to Dienogest/DMSO, Dienogest/DMF, Dienogest/MeOH, Dienogest/NMP.
#
# Starting geometry: Dienogest = the r2SCAN-3c-level gas-phase optimized
#   geometry (Dienogest/Gas/DienogestGasOptFreq.xyz, converged), same basis
#   as used for the MeOH and NMP builds (NOTE: the earlier DMSO/DMF builds
#   used a different, XTB2-level Dienogest geometry - this basis
#   inconsistency across the 5 solvents may itself be worth revisiting when
#   comparing the final results).
# Acetone: the REAL r2SCAN-3c/SMD(acetone)-optimized monomer geometry
#   (Acetone/r2SCAN3c/Monomer_r2SCAN3c_SMD.xyz, converged, E = -193.119405
#   Eh) - not an unoptimized guess.
#
# Dienogest centroid = (-5.521, 1.467, -0.724); max atom-centroid distance =
#   6.24 Ang.
# Acetone's own extent from its O reference atom = 3.10 Ang.
# 10 Acetone molecules placed at offset 9.5 Ang from Dienogest's centroid,
#   along the same 12 directions used throughout this project, each rotated
#   so the molecule's bulk (the two methyl groups) points radially outward.
# Cell Sphere radius set to 14.0 Ang.
# Checked: min Acetone-Dienogest atom distance = 3.81 Ang (no clash), max
#   atom distance from the sphere center = 12.27 Ang (safely inside the
#   14.0 Ang sphere). Total atom count = 148 (48 + 10x10), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere -5.521, 1.467, -0.724, 14.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Dienogest_10Acetone_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

